# L §6.1 (round 14): "Currencies are one by their code in the joint model and in every member ...; two
# declarations of one code with different minor units are refused (LOAD-SAME)"; L §8.3 "currency <C> is declared with
# different minor units by <a> and <b>". a declares PLN minor 0.01, b minor 1. (Writer 6's U-33.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "e438b0e9e801813f005290db20ae57dbafcfc06810324f3ba998080e5c2db6c3"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "32f97f3c875307c22a6794a75dc23dca057b147336e8fe2cbe5e858805da7f8a"

ask r: a.income[a.ana]
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
place wsp: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input income[p in persons]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ana, ola] lives 2000-01-01..
  income[ana] = 100.00 PLN "umowa"
  income[ola] = 10.00 PLN "umowa"
  opening[wsp] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 1
kind persons
place wsp: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input pocket[p in persons]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ben, ola_k] lives 2000-01-01..
  pocket[ben] = 50 PLN "umowa"
  pocket[ola_k] = 5 PLN "umowa"
  opening[wsp] = 1 000 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SAME currency PLN is declared with different minor units by a and b ...
